# Kalshibot Operating Contract (Locked — April 2026)

Expert full-stack quant work on **Kalshibot** only: local-first, self-hosted Kalshi trading.

## Locked project shape

- **Stack:** FastAPI (async) + React/Vite/TypeScript + Recharts.
- **Engines:** Five visible — **Live**, **Lab A (staging)**, **Labs B/C/D (breeders)**. **Labs Breeding v0.1:** up to six **`lab_child_*`** engines inside **`dual_engine_loop`** (hidden from main branch strip).
- **Config:** JSON rules + sizing in SQLite; **every config save** must go through **`config_history`** (audit trail).
- **Optimizer:** Internal pulse is default/safe; Claude path optional and must stay separated from internal pulse in optimizer/breeding code.

## Non-negotiable safety (never violate)

- **Only Lab A** may be promoted to Live.
- **Real money:** explicit user confirmation + **`live_paper_trading=false` / `simulate=false`** gates intact; never remove or weaken confirm paths.
- **Never weaken:** patient stop-loss, promotion workflow, or any safety gate touching Live.

## Breeding system

- **Breeders:** Labs B/C/D. **Children:** `lab_child_1`…`lab_child_6` via mutation + crossover; run in dual loop; track lineage, fitness (advanced replay metrics), death chamber.
- **Breeder UI:** 12-axis personality radar and related readouts from **`GET /api/optimizer/status`** (with dashboard Optimizer vs Breeder modes).
- **Adoption** of children into Lab A **remains gated** (no shortcuts).

## Versioning (operator default)

- **`VERSION` + `CHANGELOG`:** After **v0.4**, routine releases increment the **patch** under 0.4 (**`v0.4.01`**, **`v0.4.02`**, …). Use a **bump** (e.g. next **`v0.5`**) only when the operator explicitly asks to bump the minor/major line.

## Parallel `main` + `develop` (local)

- Optional **git worktree** + scripts under **`scripts/`** (`setup-main-worktree.ps1`, `bootstrap-main-worktree.ps1`, `launch_local.ps1`, `launch-main-sidecar.ps1`): separate **ports** and **`data/`** per checkout (`SQLITE_PATH` / `DATA_LOG_DIR` relative paths resolve per repo root); avoid two processes **posting live orders** with the same Kalshi credentials unless that is intentional.

## Implementation discipline

- **Backend:** Pydantic v2, structlog, DI where the codebase already uses it; engines stay in **`engine.py`** / **`dual_engine_loop`**; breeding logic in **`lab_breeding.py`** / optimizer modules — clear separation internal pulse vs Claude.
- **Tests:** Money-path and stop-loss tests **must stay green** after changes.
- **Style:** Observability-first (logs, status routes, dashboard); **conservative defaults**; prefer **config-driven** changes over hard-coded logic.
- **Comments:** Add clear notes for non-obvious breeding, mutation, fitness, or risk logic.
- **Frontend:** Clean, informative, responsive; **radar charts** (Optimizer Thinking + Breeder) are central.

Preserve **multi-lab + breeding** architecture in every edit. Be precise, defensive, production-minded, and paranoid about anything that touches real money.
